00:38:55.190 --> 00:39:00.920
and let's say I sell 10 billion pairs of sneakers, there

00:39:00.940 --> 00:39:06.779
might be another brand out there who is envious of my brand.

00:39:06.799 --> 00:39:09.769
But at the end of the day, they are still only selling 10

00:39:09.769 --> 00:39:10.769
pairs of sneakers.

00:39:10.769 --> 00:39:13.769
So I am not going to put too much emphasis on my

00:39:13.769 --> 00:39:17.139
competitors, and I always knew that as well as a brand. I

00:39:17.159 --> 00:39:20.009
know my brand. So when there is negative feedback, I also

00:39:20.029 --> 00:39:25.789
consider the source of the feedback and are they truly a fan

00:39:25.809 --> 00:39:30.349
or the product or competition. And if it's competition, then

00:39:30.369 --> 00:39:34.079
I address it in one aspect and hopefully give them enough

00:39:34.099 --> 00:39:38.289
information to give them a new perspective. But if it's a

00:39:38.309 --> 00:39:43.079
fan, I try to give them enough information to alleviate any

00:39:43.099 --> 00:39:48.579
fears so that they can continue to engage for the whole

00:39:48.599 --> 00:39:51.900
ride, the whole story. So that's how I utilize social media.

00:39:51.920 --> 00:39:58.659
I am there for - again, whether it's good, bad or otherwise

00:39:58.679 --> 00:40:01.569
but I am wise enough to pick and choose on who I engage

00:40:01.569 --> 00:40:05.869
with. So if I choose to engage you, that means that I see a

00:40:05.889 --> 00:40:13.739
tremendous upside in answering your challenge and answering

00:40:13.759 --> 00:40:17.630
the competitiveness because I believe that my brand overall

00:40:17.650 --> 00:40:21.420
and in the marathon of it all, in the long term, that I will

00:40:21.440 --> 00:40:26.819
come out shining on the other side. So that's kind of my

00:40:26.839 --> 00:40:53.860
approach to that.

00:40:53.880 --> 00:40:54.880
[Audience]

00:40:54.880 --> 00:40:58.079
Well, the reason why I put the word 'marathon' out in front

00:40:58.099 --> 00:41:01.360
of branding is that you have to be committed, because the

00:41:01.380 --> 00:41:03.819
initial feedback when you start to define the brand

00:41:03.839 --> 00:41:07.829
initially may not be when you thought. You may not get to

00:41:07.849 --> 00:41:11.989
the desired results initially. People may not know who you

00:41:12.009 --> 00:41:15.199
are. Another good example, if we just use musicians, in this

00:41:15.219 --> 00:41:22.279
case is Nicki Minaj. So who she is today is not who she was

00:41:22.299 --> 00:41:27.969
when she first started. But at some point, if you Google her

00:41:27.989 --> 00:41:30.859
and look at her history, you will see that she started to

00:41:30.859 --> 00:41:34.969
introduce more characteristics of who she is as she went

00:41:34.989 --> 00:41:40.389
along. And I remember in our house early on, I told two of

00:41:40.409 --> 00:41:46.360
my daughters that I like Nicki Minaj, which for them it was

00:41:46.380 --> 00:41:53.860
like, "Dad, what, what, you know dad." I said, initially, I

00:41:53.880 --> 00:41:56.909
see a whole lot of talent there, is what I told my

00:41:56.929 --> 00:41:59.929
daughters. I said, "I am not listening to every word she is

00:41:59.929 --> 00:42:02.679
rapping right now, that you listen to every word. Daddy is

00:42:02.679 --> 00:42:05.429
not listening to every word." I am looking at talent right

00:42:05.429 --> 00:42:11.000
here. And I felt as though because in my household as a

00:42:11.019 --> 00:42:15.759
father, I am putting my other hat on, I am raising five kids

00:42:15.779 --> 00:42:19.589
and two nephews. So I am not the biggest fan of a tremendous

00:42:19.609 --> 00:42:22.449
amount of profanity being thrown around my house that's

00:42:22.469 --> 00:42:23.900
there.

00:42:23.920 --> 00:42:29.449
So when they heard me say I like Nicki Minaj early, her

00:42:29.469 --> 00:42:32.579
early music, they were like there but you don't always

00:42:32.599 --> 00:42:33.599
subscribe to

00:42:33.599 --> 00:42:36.579
[inaudible]. Well, that's not what I am telling you. What I

00:42:36.579 --> 00:42:39.829
am telling is I am seeing other people attack who she is, is

00:42:39.829 --> 00:42:43.380
what I said at that time. And I said, but I see a greater

00:42:43.400 --> 00:42:49.239
brand down the road. And I am certainly not architect but I

00:42:49.259 --> 00:42:54.759
have watched her evolve into what I thought she could become

00:42:54.779 --> 00:42:57.119
[inaudible] really is to her because I see that she is very

00:42:57.119 --> 00:43:02.699
independent, and she asserts herself. And so what I am

00:43:02.719 --> 00:43:05.909
really saying is that initially, the feedback that you are

00:43:05.929 --> 00:43:09.049
looking for might not be the feedback that you get but you

00:43:09.069 --> 00:43:11.759
have to be willing to run the marathon.

00:43:11.779 --> 00:43:16.639
Now, in music, that's tough because there is a tremendous

00:43:16.659 --> 00:43:20.250
amount of pressure to make quarterly numbers, which is what

00:43:20.269 --> 00:43:24.670
helped run the music business because we went from, I want

00:43:24.690 --> 00:43:30.630
to make a great album and I put 14 songs on. And song #1 and

00:43:30.650 --> 00:43:34.789
song #14 actually connect. There is a story here. But when

00:43:34.809 --> 00:43:38.719
they introduced first week numbers, they changed the entire

00:43:38.739 --> 00:43:43.440
music business. They changed it to a game of sport of who

00:43:43.460 --> 00:43:48.179
hits the most homeruns in the first week, not even in the

00:43:48.199 --> 00:43:51.789
season. You may hit 10 homeruns the first week and that's

00:43:51.809 --> 00:43:55.389
it. At the end of the year, how many did you hit, 10. But

00:43:55.409 --> 00:43:58.239
they wanted to make quarterly numbers, they needed to. And

00:43:58.259 --> 00:44:01.009
so they put the emphasis on the first week, the first

00:44:01.009 --> 00:44:04.440
quarter, is what they were trying to do. And so now, you had

00:44:04.460 --> 00:44:05.960
to pay for point of purchase.

00:44:05.960 --> 00:44:10.639
So stores like - and it wasn't obviously just Best Buy at

00:44:10.659 --> 00:44:13.909
the time because I am going all the way back - but Best Buy

00:44:13.909 --> 00:44:17.159
had to charge you for point of purchase. So if you want that

00:44:17.159 --> 00:44:19.909
new album out front for the first week, you want counter

00:44:19.909 --> 00:44:22.909
space. It was 50 cents what is counter space now it's $2

00:44:22.909 --> 00:44:25.329
because you want it for this week. So that changed the

00:44:25.329 --> 00:44:28.449
dynamic. So now, the record companies could no longer stick

00:44:28.469 --> 00:44:32.500
with an artist for the marathon for their brand because they

00:44:32.519 --> 00:44:36.049
had to make first quarter number. So you wouldn't have had

00:44:36.069 --> 00:44:39.779
the opportunity which again is kudos to Cash Money in their

00:44:39.799 --> 00:44:47.130
company and Birdman because who Nicki is, they allowed her

00:44:47.150 --> 00:44:49.420
and stuck with it and watch the brand grow.

00:44:49.440 --> 00:44:53.719
So the parallel for you is - I am making the analogy of

00:44:53.739 --> 00:44:58.039
making is that even if you don't get the feedback initially,

00:44:58.059 --> 00:45:00.480
if you determine from the beginning that you want to be in

00:45:00.480 --> 00:45:04.119
it for this brand for the marathon, then it allows you to

00:45:04.139 --> 00:45:05.259
get the feedback, being

00:45:05.279 --> 00:45:10.089
[inaudible], change some of the characteristics based upon

00:45:10.109 --> 00:45:13.549
the feedback from the community and the crowd not for

00:45:13.569 --> 00:45:17.449
competitors. This is most important for the music business.

00:45:17.469 --> 00:45:22.769
Most of the fans and followers on certain sites all want to

00:45:22.789 --> 00:45:27.150
be musicians. So you are never going to get - nobody is

00:45:27.170 --> 00:45:30.960
getting five stars because most of the fans around those

00:45:30.980 --> 00:45:35.380
sites want to be the artists. But if you can carve out who

00:45:35.400 --> 00:45:38.619
actually likes the artist, you can look at the analytics and

00:45:38.639 --> 00:45:42.980
tell who really is Genie Wine, and the affection for that

00:45:43.000 --> 00:45:45.960
artist, then you can begin to shape the brand a little

00:45:45.980 --> 00:45:49.150
better. So I hope that answered some of what you were

00:45:49.170 --> 00:45:50.170
asking.

00:45:50.170 --> 00:45:51.170
[Audience]

00:45:51.170 --> 00:46:09.049
Well, today, again, we have to be sensitive because we are

00:46:09.069 --> 00:46:12.779
streaming. So even when I just named some of the names, I

00:46:12.799 --> 00:46:16.659
was being sensitive to fans and businesspeople affiliating

00:46:16.679 --> 00:46:21.210
associated, watching and maybe not understating we are doing

00:46:21.230 --> 00:46:27.019
strictly business. But right now, in that space, in the

00:46:27.039 --> 00:46:31.849
space of entertainment, characters probably are working

00:46:31.869 --> 00:46:35.589
better. Again, if you look at top 10 artists and you point

00:46:35.609 --> 00:46:38.449
out the characteristics of the top five, those are not

00:46:38.469 --> 00:46:42.049
normal people walking around that are going to walk and sit

00:46:42.069 --> 00:46:45.319
next to you in the way that they either address or they are

00:46:45.319 --> 00:46:48.230
positioning. So right now, to cut through, you might want to

00:46:48.250 --> 00:46:52.159
get a purple hat and pink shirt and some green shoes just to

00:46:52.179 --> 00:46:55.319
walk and catch everybody's attention. And then once you get

00:46:55.339 --> 00:46:58.710
their attention, because again we are talking about marathon

00:46:58.730 --> 00:47:01.569
and the whole person, you start to introduce the other

00:47:01.589 --> 00:47:05.319
characteristics. Again, if you go back, Lady Gaga day one to

00:47:05.339 --> 00:47:08.929
Lady Gaga today with an agenda, a political position, a

00:47:08.949 --> 00:47:13.900
social position, mobilized, crowdsource, audience, monsters,

00:47:13.920 --> 00:47:19.940
little masters, this is who I am, all of that now from here.

00:47:19.960 --> 00:47:26.170
So characters could be very powerful as long as you don't

00:47:26.190 --> 00:47:30.259
overdo it for the long haul. So that's going to be it, don't

00:47:30.279 --> 00:47:33.779
overdo it for the long haul, and they do it on their own. I

00:47:33.779 --> 00:47:36.029
am watching from an artistic standpoint. The artists who

00:47:36.029 --> 00:47:39.250
take their character to a certain point - I have got a bunch

00:47:39.269 --> 00:47:43.599
of keys so I understand - the characters, they will take it

00:47:43.619 --> 00:47:46.469
to a certain point, then they pull back on their own now,

00:47:46.469 --> 00:47:50.210
like - and not to overemphasize it. But Lady Gaga said, "

00:47:50.230 --> 00:47:53.980
This is who I am, this is who I am. Wait a minute, I don't

00:47:53.980 --> 00:47:56.480
like you. You are talking negative against a certain group

00:47:56.480 --> 00:48:01.009
of individuals, and I want my voice heard." So characters

00:48:01.029 --> 00:48:04.880
step aside, and now the woman would like to say something to

00:48:04.900 --> 00:48:07.449
you. I don't agree with your message and here is my message,

00:48:07.449 --> 00:48:10.539
I am going to defend this particular cause or group.

00:48:10.559 --> 00:48:14.839
So I watch artists today. They all create a character but

00:48:14.859 --> 00:48:17.279
then they will also step outside of the character and deal

00:48:17.279 --> 00:48:21.969
with issues. Unlike previously, we have had in the last 10

00:48:21.989 --> 00:48:25.719
years certain athletes who never addressed one issue, who

00:48:25.739 --> 00:48:29.949
had all of voice could have address issues, could have been

00:48:29.969 --> 00:48:33.250
very helpful in a lot of ways. But if you look at their

00:48:33.269 --> 00:48:38.309
history, they never addressed one issue. They were happy to

00:48:38.329 --> 00:48:41.489
be athlete. They remained --

00:48:41.509 --> 00:48:42.509
[Informal Talk]

00:48:42.509 --> 00:48:47.349
Well, there is a couple of them though but they remain

00:48:47.369 --> 00:48:50.380
nameless, and that's okay because again, it can't be forced

00:48:50.400 --> 00:48:55.670
upon you. You can't join your activism class and say, "I am

00:48:55.690 --> 00:48:58.799
an activist," and you walk around Stanford all day to send

00:48:58.819 --> 00:49:01.069
your activism, somebody would say, "Well, what's your issue?

00:49:01.069 --> 00:49:05.519
" "I am an activist." It's not going to work too long. You

00:49:05.539 --> 00:49:10.039
have to really have an idea and issue, it has to be organic

00:49:10.059 --> 00:49:11.059
to be engaging.

00:49:11.059 --> 00:49:12.059
[Audience]

00:49:12.059 --> 00:49:42.059
Well, for me, personally, I really view the world as real,

00:50:01.900 --> 00:50:07.769
real time, actual real time. And again, I am also keenly and

00:50:07.789 --> 00:50:13.469
acutely aware that the National Archives bought the Twitter

00:50:13.489 --> 00:50:19.259
[inaudible]. You do know that. So every twit is being held

00:50:19.279 --> 00:50:22.739
forever and

00:50:22.759 --> 00:50:25.509
[inaudible], all of you twits, not some of them, every one

00:50:25.529 --> 00:50:28.549
of them wanting to the national historic archives to be

00:50:28.569 --> 00:50:34.650
recalled 500 years from now, and I am aware of that. So for

00:50:34.670 --> 00:50:40.650
me, if I twit it, I can stand by it. If I twit it even as a

00:50:40.670 --> 00:50:45.489
joke, I can live with it because one of the things that I am

00:50:45.509 --> 00:50:49.819
emphasizing as a personal brand and marathon branding is I

00:50:49.839 --> 00:50:53.549
am effused to be one thing because I don't know anybody who

00:50:53.569 --> 00:50:58.359
is just one thing. Even if you look at all of your heroes

00:50:58.379 --> 00:51:02.299
historically, we know that they all had flaws. So I don't

00:51:02.319 --> 00:51:06.879
want to be the flawless hero or Mr. Perfect. None of those

00:51:06.899 --> 00:51:10.929
guys or brands will survive in today's real-time world.

00:51:10.949 --> 00:51:14.859
The new heroes will be the heroes that have flaws. That's

00:51:14.879 --> 00:51:17.589
the new heroes, why, because they really like you, they are

00:51:17.589 --> 00:51:21.969
closer to you. So the old positioning of creating this

00:51:21.989 --> 00:51:27.839
character, spotless, sinless, blah, blah, blah, it won't

00:51:27.859 --> 00:51:32.599
work. And if you take that position, you don't have to

00:51:32.619 --> 00:51:34.869
overanalyze every twit. You don't have to worry about

00:51:34.869 --> 00:51:37.869
everybody do they agree with it. And by the way, say you

00:51:37.869 --> 00:51:40.869
guys are going to run enterprise, and you are going to run

00:51:40.869 --> 00:51:43.489
the new businesses, you also won't judge your employees the

00:51:43.489 --> 00:51:47.119
way they are saying you want to be a judged. In other words,

00:51:47.139 --> 00:51:49.889
what are they telling you that you better be careful of

00:51:49.889 --> 00:51:52.639
everything you say on Facebook and on Twitter and all of

00:51:52.639 --> 00:51:55.639
that because when you go and you put your resume, and they

00:51:55.639 --> 00:51:58.639
are going to be viewing, and they are going to see that's

00:51:58.639 --> 00:52:02.139
you and you are not going to get a job, well it depends on

00:52:02.139 --> 00:52:05.139
who is going to be reviewing. If that person also twits and

00:52:05.139 --> 00:52:08.139
has Facebook and has said something, they are going to go I

00:52:08.139 --> 00:52:10.639
have said 20 things I wish I could take back.

00:52:10.639 --> 00:52:13.889
So in the future, it won't be as sensitive an issue. But in

00:52:13.889 --> 00:52:16.889
answer to your question, James, my thing is to be whole and

00:52:16.889 --> 00:52:23.779
to be full or possible flaws. That's the journey; that's the

00:52:23.799 --> 00:52:28.629
journey. In this room, if you haven't made any mistakes, you

00:52:28.649 --> 00:52:32.469
wouldn't be here right now. The fact that you are here is

00:52:32.489 --> 00:52:35.759
the product of some mistakes that you have made, and yet you

00:52:35.779 --> 00:52:39.619
ended up here each and every one of you guys. So branding

00:52:39.639 --> 00:52:42.440
really is - marathon branding is about understanding that

00:52:42.460 --> 00:52:46.379
from the beginning. Build that into who you are, build that

00:52:46.399 --> 00:52:51.179
into your brand, listen, I am not flawless but I can tell

00:52:51.199 --> 00:52:57.549
you that if we were to argue, Republican and Democrats, I

00:52:57.569 --> 00:53:00.559
have said before the election, I said wow, Republicans won't

00:53:00.579 --> 00:53:04.359
get this back for 16 years. Sam, what are you talking about,

00:53:04.379 --> 00:53:07.379
they haven't even lost a person for four years. I said no,

00:53:07.379 --> 00:53:10.079
they won't get it back, why, because they are pointing out

00:53:10.079 --> 00:53:14.579
every flaw of everybody that they can. And then what that

00:53:14.599 --> 00:53:16.650
does is

00:53:16.670 --> 00:53:18.739
[inaudible] because now, they turn the camera back and say,

00:53:18.739 --> 00:53:23.529
oh, you did this and you are saying that his platform is not

00:53:23.549 --> 00:53:27.409
the one I should vote for because he is not flawless.

00:53:27.429 --> 00:53:31.969
Well, you see what happened with that was even two years in,

00:53:31.989 --> 00:53:37.389
I want to see your birth certificate. It's the way it works.

00:53:37.409 --> 00:53:40.299
Once you start focusing on

00:53:40.319 --> 00:53:43.609
[inaudible], I am going to find a flaw, even recently you

00:53:43.629 --> 00:53:47.670
mentioned it earlier, Jason and you

00:53:47.690 --> 00:53:50.059
[inaudible] I won't pull that name back out but name started

00:53:50.059 --> 00:53:53.480
saying again, I am going to go to this issue, that issue got

00:53:53.500 --> 00:53:56.409
handled, and what's the next issue. Let me see the academic

00:53:56.409 --> 00:54:01.089
record. It's nonsense. This is not what we are about in this

00:54:01.109 --> 00:54:03.889
generation. We want substance. We live in a real time. We

00:54:03.909 --> 00:54:07.159
want to know how we are going to fix and solve problems and

00:54:07.159 --> 00:54:10.159
issues, and no one person or one man has to but the

00:54:10.159 --> 00:54:14.539
community can solve because the other side of social media -

00:54:14.559 --> 00:54:17.480
and I am setting aside branding right now, I am just talking

00:54:17.480 --> 00:54:20.309
specifically social media - is that now we can crowdsource

00:54:20.329 --> 00:54:24.150
information from the world. So all of this distant learning,

00:54:24.170 --> 00:54:28.159
all of these brands are all now connected. So when we say

00:54:28.179 --> 00:54:31.659
solve it, it's not just solve it me, it's not just solve it

00:54:31.659 --> 00:54:35.449
Stanford, it's all of us solve it and we are all connected,

00:54:35.469 --> 00:54:38.949
and we can give input. It's a whole new world, it's a whole

00:54:38.949 --> 00:54:51.500
new place, a whole new paradigm shift.

00:54:51.519 --> 00:54:52.519
[Audience]

00:54:52.519 --> 00:54:57.989
So for my daughter Kiba's personal brand, so she is

00:54:58.009 --> 00:55:01.809
[inaudible]. She graduated from the University of Texas last

00:55:01.829 --> 00:55:14.559
year.

00:55:14.579 --> 00:55:15.579
[Informal Talk]

00:55:15.579 --> 00:55:28.629
What I hope for Kiba, well what I am doing is that Kiba is

00:55:28.649 --> 00:55:35.409
comfortable enough that she is taking my advice to feel like

00:55:35.429 --> 00:55:38.989
she is not under any pressure to be anything other than

00:55:39.009 --> 00:55:42.559
whatever she wants to be, whatever she wants to do, but

00:55:42.579 --> 00:55:51.039
utilize these tools. I mean she is --

00:55:51.059 --> 00:55:52.059
[Informal Talk]

00:55:52.059 --> 00:55:56.190
She is 23 now. You are saying in the operated 18, so I know

00:55:56.210 --> 00:55:58.230
you can sing, you

00:55:58.250 --> 00:56:01.339
[inaudible]. You got two degrees in four years so I know you

00:56:01.359 --> 00:56:06.230
can think. So she is academic, and you always have been very

00:56:06.250 --> 00:56:11.139
independent. You have left, graduated and went to Spain for

00:56:11.159 --> 00:56:15.269
six months. I had a concert in Belgium, and you showed up.

00:56:15.289 --> 00:56:21.239
You navigated through Europe by yourself. So --

00:56:21.259 --> 00:56:22.259
[Informal Talk]

00:56:22.259 --> 00:56:25.699
So I know you know how to navigate the world. I know you

00:56:25.719 --> 00:56:28.170
have talents and gifts and everything. So my dream for you

00:56:28.170 --> 00:56:33.059
is whatever makes you happy but do it, just do it, do it

00:56:33.079 --> 00:56:36.519
comfortably. That's what I hope for her brand. I hope that

00:56:36.539 --> 00:56:39.949
brand ultimately really means to somebody that you are

00:56:39.969 --> 00:56:43.629
[inaudible] that you will impact the world from humanity

00:56:43.649 --> 00:56:47.589
standpoint. No matter what the gifts you use, at the end,

00:56:47.609 --> 00:56:50.929
they will also say she is a good person, she helped them do

00:56:50.949 --> 00:56:59.339
